From 3c2092fb34d91ed552334137d42c49886ce63da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <s.salkimbaev@abaiuniversity.edu.kz>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:43:14 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll/server: Implement wait completion packets + ALPC
 integration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements NtCreateWaitCompletionPacket, NtAssociateWaitCompletionPacket
and NtCancelWaitCompletionPacket (previously absent in Wine), backed by a
new server-side wait_completion_packet object. When an associated target
object signals, an I/O completion packet is posted to the bound completion
port — the mechanism WinAppSDK CoreMessaging uses to service its in-process
ALPC registrar.

ALPC server ports now notify associated wait completion packets when a
connection request arrives, so a CoreMessaging-style registrar parked on
NtRemoveIoCompletionEx wakes, receives the connection via
NtAlpcSendWaitReceivePort and accepts it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
